<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chiang Kai-shek</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a>–<a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chiang Kai-shek was a Chinese military and political leader who headed the Nationalist Party, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen</a>. Commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-expedition">Northern Expedition</a>, he established the Nationalist Government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> in 1928, fought the Communists and regional rivals, and led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1937. Defeated in the civil war, he moved the government of the Republic of China to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> in 1949 and ruled there until his death.</p></div>
